A||N||18||kevin||slow acceration||||1||
Z||000000||kevin||03-05-2000||01:37 AM||||O.k fellas, this is my first visit. Based on my previous month of logging on, I learned more than many auto shop workers. Heres my dilema. I have a '85 SE. I recently had a complete tune up. Nevertheless, as I try to merge onto the freeway, I just wont go fast. The accelerator is almost floored, yet I have difficulty reaching 65 mph! Any suggestions? Oh yes, I did have the catalytic converter checked as well.   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||03-05-2000||04:41 AM||||did you change the fuel filter? when the filter gets dirty you start losing performance.||||reg||1
Z||000002||b_b_a_d||03-05-2000||08:59 AM||||Is it the iron duke, or a v6?<P>Just what is the average performance of a 4 cylinder anyway???  <P>This was sort of meant as a joke, but the truth is I'm not familiar with the output of a 4 cylinder.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 03-05-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||batboy||03-05-2000||09:00 AM||||And air filter too. Fieros like to go through spark plug wires pretty fast, this is consider part of a tune up in my book, how long has it been? Compression check is another recommendation.||||reg||1
Z||000004||b_b_a_d||03-05-2000||09:12 AM||||automatic or manual?<P>You mentioned the pedal almost all the way to the floor???  What about all the way to the floor!  Work with me here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Trixi||03-05-2000||09:35 AM||||Here's a suggestion!  Check to see if it isn't losing fire or cross-firing. My 84 tends to do that, especially when it is wet.  This will definitely cause it to accelerate slow and not reach top speed! ||||reg||3
Z||000006||batboy||03-05-2000||09:44 AM||||Trixi, if your car is cross-firing when it's wet, you probably need new plug wires too.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87SC/GT||03-05-2000||10:13 AM||||"Tune up" is a very broad description. If the timing was altered I would go back and recheck it. Make sure it is advancing properly. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||kevin||03-06-2000||12:38 AM||||I want to thank all those who answerd. The detail I omited are (A.) 4 cyl.(B.)117,000 mi.(C.) 5 sp. Here's what I did so far: 1.) new fuel filter 2.) new plugs, wires and cap 3.)new air filter 4.) recent GM dealership recall work-- it was never done before!5.) new distributor[control modulator & pick-up coil] 6.)timing checked 7.)new O2 sensor 8.) new idle air control. Please administer any wisdom. I can't go faster than 75mph! I also checked the Thermac controll valve, it works.      ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shiner||03-06-2000||02:48 AM||||How about the throttle cable?  I burned one out in my '84 SC one time.  It goes right over the exhaust manifold, and that plastic sleave just melted.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||03-06-2000||03:01 AM||||I own a 84 fiero with the four cylinder and its an automatic, i got it up to more then 85mph with it red lining.<P>First, is your car running okay in the other gears?  Is your acceleration fine in the first gear?  NO hesitations, backfiring.<P>How old are your plug wires, if you do buy the cheap ones, I have before, my fiero will dry them out really quick.  Did you gap your plugs, and buy autolites or champions, dont get plantinums.  When you drive in first gear and floor it, does the engine sound strong?<P>You can check if your valves are back if you stick a dollar bill on your exhaust pipe and if the dollar bill is getting sucked in you might need a valve job.<P>Check your pcv valve, if it rattles then its good, and if the pipe sucks.  Check if your egr valve isn't getting stuck, you can stick your finger in there and your car will try to die out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Brian84SE||03-06-2000||08:17 PM||||How about a clogged catalytic converter?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Bob Englert||03-06-2000||08:54 PM||||I had a similar problem with my 88 Formula when I bought it.  It had no kick and felt like it was choking itself.  It turned out to be the converter was shot and clogging the exhaust.  New cat and muffler made a BIG difference.||||reg||1
Z||000013||kevin||03-07-2000||02:22 AM||||All good suggestion from everybody. Today I advanced the timingto about 10 deg. It seemed to help a little. Here's a thought that has put a burr in my saddle, when I first replaced the distributor, I noted the position for easy replacement @ 12:00. When I dropped the distributor back in it was now closer to 11:00-rotor pointing to cyl.It is possible I alterd the timing enough where the car still "runs" yet is either too far advanced or retarded to provide efficient combustion hence a lack of power? ||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||03-07-2000||06:40 PM||||Yes. you can have it way off and still start it. It'll run like crap.<P>speeder, 85mph at redline? is that all? You must have had the worst set of gears ever put in a TH125. I'm doing at least 90 and only at 3500. I haven't done the headlight thing so I've never tried to max it.||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||03-07-2000||07:33 PM||||Are you SURE your cat isn't clogged?  If it's the original at 117K, I'd replace it.  Who checked it for you, and how?<P>When I bought my 88 Coupe with 68K miles, it seemed to lack power at high RPM and sputter under load at lower RPM (like climbing hills on the freeway in  5th gear).  The cat was clogged and it had two leaky vaccuum lines.  Fixed those and it's been pretty quick ever since (well, for a Duke, that is).||||reg||3
Z||000016||Formula||03-07-2000||08:35 PM||||WOW ogre, my V6 runs 3500 at 90 mph, I didnt know that the duke was that powerful.<P>Would that mean we have the same set of gears? ||||reg||1
Z||000017||fierospeeder||03-07-2000||10:13 PM||||my speedometer pegs at 85, but i know im going faster then that.  <BR>I do need another gear. 3 isn't enough.<BR>I think the stock hp of the duke is 92hp.<P>My moms car is the 2.8 and its an automatic, i got it pegging at 85 also, its also a 3 speed and i do need another gear.  I have no idea what the top speed im getting.<P>I know you cant really count by rpms because you have to base it on horsepower also, if the horsepower isn't that great and you have a heavy car, and going more then 100, the car is also fighting aerodynamics.  Ive done this on my other car, Im going about 100 estimate at 3000 rpms and i got 3000 more but my car cant push enough on the taller gear.||||reg||1
Z||000018||kevin||03-08-2000||01:46 AM||||One of the joy of owning a Fiero,in reality there are thousands of happy moments,(other plebian drivers just can't comprehend),is when the Fiero seem to "fix" themselves. Then love starts all over again. This seems to be the case of my slow accelerating 85 'Duke'.On my way to work today the power apppears to have resurfaced. For no logical rason! What gives? Bad gas? New plugs that eventually burned up excess carbon deposits? I am going to keep everybody posted. Again, I really appreciate all your suggestions. ||||reg||7
